(\\subsection{Migration and remittance-dependent demand}) Tj
T* (Bihar's labor markets are deeply shaped by circular and long-term migration. Migration) Tj
T* (functions as a private insurance mechanism, a labor market equilibrium margin, and a) Tj
T* (transmission channel for macro shocks. Remittance income supports consumption smoothing, human) Tj
T* (capital spending, and housing investment, but can also mask weak local job creation. Any Bihar) Tj
T* (growth model that ignores migration mis-specifies labor supply dynamics and household demand) Tj
T* (multipliers.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Agrarian constraints and climate exposure}) Tj
T* (Agriculture remains central to livelihoods, yet faces fragmentation, variable irrigation) Tj
T* (quality, input-price volatility, and high climate sensitivity. Floods, erratic monsoon) Tj
T* (behavior, and heat stress generate output fluctuations with spillovers to rural wages, credit) Tj
T* (stress, and nutrition outcomes. Thus climate risk is not an environmental externality at the) Tj
T* (edge of macroeconomics; it is a first-order macro driver for Bihar.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Public finance and state capacity}) Tj
T* (Bihar's ability to finance and execute growth-oriented public investment depends on own-tax) Tj
T* (effort, transfer architecture, borrowing space, and project implementation quality. The) Tj
T* (development literature increasingly emphasizes that the growth effect of public capital is) Tj
T* (mediated by state capacity: procurement integrity, engineering quality, maintenance systems,) Tj
T* (and accountability institutions. We incorporate this via efficiency-adjusted public capital.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\section{Literature Review: Global and Indian Evidence}) Tj
T* (\\subsection{Convergence, fundamentals, and conditional catch-up}) Tj
T* (The neoclassical growth literature predicts convergence conditional on savings, population) Tj
T* (growth, and technology adoption \\citep{solow1956,swan1956,mankiw1992}. Cross-country evidence) Tj
T* (suggests partial convergence rather than universal equalization, consistent with institutional) Tj
T* (and policy heterogeneity \\citep{barro1991,islam1995}. For subnational units, convergence can) Tj
T* (be weaker when labor mobility and market integration are incomplete or when initial capability) Tj
T* (gaps persist.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Endogenous growth and innovation complementarities}) Tj
T* (Endogenous growth theory demonstrates how ideas, knowledge spillovers, and human capital can) Tj
T* (sustain long-run growth without diminishing returns in the aggregate) Tj
T* (\\citep{romer1986,romer1990,lucas1988,aghion1992}. For frontier and near-frontier regions,) Tj
T* (innovation systems are central. For lagging regions such as Bihar, adaptation, diffusion,) Tj
T* (management quality, and organizational capability are often more binding than original) Tj
T* (invention.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Structural transformation and dual economy dynamics}) Tj
T* (Lewis-type dual economy models emphasize labor transfer from low-productivity agriculture to) Tj
T* (higher-productivity non-farm sectors \\citep{lewis1954,fei1964}. Later evidence highlights that) Tj
T* (movement to low-productivity informal services can slow aggregate gains unless manufacturing) Tj
T* (and modern services absorb labor at scale \\citep{mcmillan2014,rodrik2016}. Bihar's) Tj
T* (transformation challenge therefore concerns \\emph{where} labor moves, not just whether it) Tj
T* (moves.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Institutions, governance, and public goods}) Tj
T* (Institutional quality is associated with long-run income differences) Tj
T* (\\citep{acemoglu2001,north1990}. At subnational levels, bureaucratic capability, contract) Tj
T* (enforcement, and local public goods provision strongly shape private investment response) Tj
T* (\\citep{besley2012,khemani2017}. Recent work in state capacity underscores that implementation) Tj
T* (quality mediates the development effects of spending \\citep{andrews2017,pritchett2018}.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Human capital quality and labor productivity}) Tj
T* (The macro returns to schooling depend on learning quality, health, and early-life nutrition) Tj
T* (\\citep{hanushek2012,heckman2006}. Cross-country and Indian evidence both show that) Tj
T* (foundational learning deficits translate into lower productivity growth and weaker structural) Tj
T* (transformation \\citep{asercentre2023,worldbank2018learning}. This is especially relevant for) Tj
T* (Bihar where enrollment gains have outpaced learning outcomes historically.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (\\subsection{Urbanization, agglomeration, and spatial frictions}) Tj
