T* (Bihar's urban transition is not yet locked into a single megacity path, which is a strategic) Tj
T* (advantage. Secondary cities can become engines of inclusive growth if municipal governance,) Tj
T* (land management, transport planning, and utility reliability are strengthened early.) Tj
T* (International evidence shows that the productivity effects of urbanization are highly) Tj
T* (sensitive to governance quality. Without planning and infrastructure coordination, urban) Tj
T* (expansion can generate congestion without agglomeration.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (An analytically useful approach is to model Bihar's cities as a system with network) Tj
