T* (\\subsection{Fiscal space, quality of spending, and intertemporal credibility}) Tj
T* (A high-growth strategy for Bihar must satisfy an intertemporal budget constraint while) Tj
T* (preserving macro credibility. Development experience suggests that growth accelerations are) Tj
T* (more durable when fiscal policy combines prudent debt management with high-quality capital) Tj
T* (spending. The composition and efficiency of spending are therefore central. A rupee spent on) Tj
T* (poorly maintained assets has low long-run multiplier value; a rupee spent on resilient and) Tj
T* (well-executed infrastructure can crowd in private investment and expand the tax base.) Tj
T* () Tj
