T* (\\subsection{Public investment management as macro policy}) Tj
T* (In many policy debates, public investment management \(PIM\) is treated as a technical) Tj
T* (governance issue rather than macroeconomics. This is a mistake. In developing regions, PIM) Tj
T* (quality determines effective capital formation and therefore potential output. Bihar's macro) Tj
T* (strategy should include institutional reforms in project appraisal, standardized procurement,) Tj
T* (independent technical review, contract management, and maintenance auditing. A state-level PIM) Tj
T* (index can be integrated into annual budgeting to align incentives.) Tj
